course: dictionary
lesson: 4082
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives a geyser three meanings, so you must use the sentence around the word to find the right one. Ask: what is the sentence about? Then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «Yellowstone, created in 1872, was the world's first national park, and it sits on top of a huge volcanic hotspot that feeds its geysers.» The words volcanic and hotspot tell you the geysers are heated from deep underground. So here a geyser is a hot spring that shoots water and steam into the air.
explain: Now read this: «The geyser is broken, so there is no hot water for the bath.» Here the clues are bath and hot water, and a geyser is a gas heater in a bathroom. This meaning is old and mostly used in the UK, so a new word may not be needed.
fact: A geyser is a hot spring in the ground that shoots hot water and steam high into the air from time to time.
fact: Geysers happen in volcanic places, where underground water is heated by hot rock until it bursts out.
fact: Famous geysers include Old Faithful in Yellowstone, USA, and Strokkur in Iceland.
fact: In the UK, an older word for a gas water heater in a kitchen or bathroom is also geyser.
fact: A geyser can mean any sudden jet of liquid shooting up, so context is needed to tell which meaning is meant.
exercise: «It sits on top of a huge volcanic hotspot that feeds its geysers.» What does geysers most likely mean here? | Signs that show the way to the car park | Tall trees growing in the park | *Hot springs that shoot water and steam into the air | Tents that visitors sleep in
exercise: «The geyser is broken, so there is no hot water for the bath.» What does geyser mean here? | A kind of volcano in Iceland | A bath toy that squirts water | A hot spring shooting steam from the ground | *A gas water heater in a bathroom
exercise: «It sits on top of a huge volcanic hotspot that feeds its geysers.» Which word is a clue that the geysers are heated from deep underground? | *volcanic | created | national | park
test: If a fire hose suddenly shoots a jet of water high into the air, could we call it a geyser? | No, because a hose is not a natural thing | *Yes, a geyser can be any sudden jet of liquid | No, only hot springs in the ground can be geysers | No, a geyser must always be made of steam
test: Strokkur is a famous geyser in which country? | Scotland | USA | New Zealand | *Iceland
exam: Why must people stay on paths near geysers? | Because geysers only come out at night | Because the paths are the only place with hot water | *Because the water is boiling hot and the ground can be thin | Because geysers are very quiet and need peace
